          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "Prayer set a hard geometry problem",
              "size": "hook",
              "at": 0.0,
              "until": 3.56
            },
            {
              "text": "Raqqa and Baghdad, the 800s",
              "sub": "al-Battani, and Abu al-Wafa after him",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 3.9,
              "until": 9.64
            },
            {
              "text": "Five times a day, face Makkah",
              "sub": "from any village on a round earth",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 9.98,
              "until": 15.69
            },
            {
              "text": "On a flat page a triangle makes 180",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 16.03,
              "until": 19.62
            },
            {
              "text": "On a ball it always makes more",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 19.96,
              "until": 23.17
            },
            {
              "text": "So the way to Makkah is an arc",
              "sub": "not a straight line on a flat map",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 23.51,
              "until": 29.44
            },
            {
              "text": "The old flat rules quietly fail",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 29.78,
              "until": 33.01
            },
            {
              "text": "So they built the maths of curves",
              "sub": "planets, oceans, orbits, signals",
